      explanation: "Total no. of employees = ` 2,400. If 40% of the no. of employees in office A are shifted equally to offices B & E. 40% of the no. of employees in office A = 126 360 40 100 2 400    ×    × , = 336 A = 336 2 = 168 are shifted equally to offices B and E Initial number of employee in office B = 2 400 18 360 , ×     = 120 Now, 120+ 168 = 288 Number of employee in office C = 2 400 54 360 , × = 360 Sum of the number of employees in B and C = 288 + 360 = 648 So, sum of the no. of employees in B and C will be 648.",
